lets crete free tier org 

Step 1 — Create the organization

1. Go to https://github.com/organizations/new
2. Choose Free plan
3. Organization name (e.g. devops-practice-org) — this becomes the URL:
   github.com/your-org-name
4. Contact email → This organization belongs to: pick "My personal account"
5. Skip the "invite members" screen for now (add them later) → Complete setup

You're now the Owner automatically.

Step 2 — Invite members (Member role)

1. Org page → People tab → Invite member
2. Enter their GitHub username or email
3. They get an invite email/notification → once accepted, they're a Member
(If you're testing solo, you can create a second free GitHub account with a different email just to practice inviting/accepting.)

Step 3 — Create some repos in the org

1. Org page → Repositories tab → New
2. Create 2–3 test repos, e.g. app-frontend, app-backend, infra-scripts

Step 4 — Create Teams

1. Org page → Teams tab → New team
2. Name it, e.g. developers
3. Add members to this team
4. Repeat for other teams — e.g. qa, release-managers

Step 5 — Give each team repo-level permission

1. Go into a Team → Repositories tab → Add repository
2. Select the repo, then set the permission level: Read / Triage / Write / Maintain / Admin
3. Do this per team per repo — e.g.:
   • developers → Write on app-frontend, app-backend
   • qa → Triage on all three
   • release-managers → Maintain on infra-scripts


Step 6 (optional) — Base permissions
Org → Settings → Member privileges → set a Base permission (e.g. Read) that applies to all members on all repos by default, before team-specific overrides kick in.















(If you're testing solo, you can create a second free GitHub account with a different email just to practice inviting/accepting.)
